# The one place yojimbo's C library dependencies are versioned.
#
# Columns: name  vendored  tag  minimum
#
#   vendored   the version of the copy in this repository (its VERSION macros)
#   tag        the upstream git tag carrying that version; the -DYOJIMBO_SYSTEM_DEPS CI job
#              installs exactly these tags, so "system dependencies" means the same version the
#              vendored build compiles
#   minimum    the floor a system-installed copy must meet, enforced at configure time
#
# netcode's floor is 1.5.0: SECURITY.md records the connect token handling that lands in
# 1.4.5, yojimbo's server config passes max_connect_token_lifetime (a field netcode 1.4.4 and
# earlier do not have), and 1.4.6 adds the eight-byte payload slack yojimbo's serialize
# BitReader requires. 1.5.0 raises the floor to the vendored version: it upgrades the wire
# protocol to NETCODE 1.03 with per-connection HChaCha20 key derivation, fixing the
# unfinished-handshake and multi-server AEAD nonce-reuse issues recorded in SECURITY.md.
# Linking an older system netcode is refused rather than warned about.
# serialize and reliable also floor at the vendored version because yojimbo's sources are
# written against it and both define wire formats.
#
# The vendored column is checked against the vendored headers at configure time, so this file
# cannot drift from the tree it describes.

serialize  2.1.3   v2.1.3   2.1.3
reliable   1.4.5   v1.4.5   1.4.5
netcode    1.5.0   v1.5.0   1.5.0
